#N canvas 20 20 1900 1200 12;
#X text 20 20 m_volca -- the Korg Volca FM \, and the only file allowed to talk to it. It is the FIRST OUTPUT-ONLY m_ layer in this project: the Volca transmits NOTHING AT ALL \, so unlike m_nano \, m_launchpad and m_organelle there are no device events to decode and nothing is ever published to param. The prefix still reads correctly -- m_ means the file that OWNS this device \, and m_launchpad already drives its own surface., f 84;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: the Pd channel that the Volca's OWN channel 1 lands on -- 49 on the Organelle \, which is input/output slot 4 per .pdsettings. REQUIRED. inlets: 3 -- see below. outlets: none \, this is a terminus., f 84;
#X text 20 240 WIRED \, NOT SENT \, AND THAT WAS A DELIBERATE DECISION. u_map reaches this file through cords from u_root rather than a global bus. param is device-to-map and disp is display \; neither fits a sounding note \, and adding a name to the allowlist is a change to ref-conventions.md rather than a local call. Cords also keep the path visible on u_root's canvas \, which is where the architecture is meant to be readable., f 84;
#X obj 20 420 inlet;
#X obj 460 420 inlet;
#X obj 900 420 inlet;
#X text 20 380 notes: <note> <vel> <dur>, f 30;
#X text 460 380 cc: <controller> <value>, f 30;
#X text 900 380 program: <n>, f 30;
#X obj 1400 420 loadbang;
#X obj 1400 470 f \$1;
#X obj 1400 520 t f f f;
#X obj 20 560 unpack f f f;
#X obj 20 700 makenote;
#X obj 20 900 noteout;
#X obj 460 560 unpack f f;
#X obj 460 640 t b f;
#X obj 460 730 f;
#X obj 460 900 ctlout;
#X obj 900 900 pgmout;
#X text 1400 580 THE CHANNEL GOES IN COLD \, off the RIGHTMOST outlets \, so all three destinations hold it before any value can arrive. Item 63 proved this pattern for midiout -- the port set into the cold inlet at load -- and it is used here for the same reason: Pd 0.49 does NOT warn about extra creation arguments \, so a clean load would prove nothing at all about a channel passed as an arg., f 60;
#X text 20 980 unpack fires RIGHT TO LEFT \, so duration and velocity are stored in makenote before the note number triggers it. makenote owns the note-offs \, which is what stops a dropped cord or a reload leaving the Volca droning., f 60;
#X text 460 1000 ⚠️ THE t b f IS LOAD-BEARING AND THE OBVIOUS WIRING IS WRONG. ctlout takes value in the HOT inlet and controller in the cold one \, but unpack emits its RIGHTMOST outlet first -- so wiring value straight through would fire ctlout while it still held the PREVIOUS controller number \, sending every CC to the wrong destination. Silent \, plausible \, and wrong. The value is parked in the f \, the controller is set from t's right outlet \, and only then does the bang release it., f 74;
#X text 900 980 ⚠️ UNVERIFIED AND IT MATTERS: whether Pd's pgmout is 0-BASED or 1-BASED on the wire. The aplaymidi tests that proved Program Change works sent RAW 0xC0 with values 0 and 20 \, which is the wire number \; if pgmout adds one \, every patch selected here is off by one and NOTHING reports it. Same shape as the 47+n pad-map error \, which looked correct and triggered the wrong drum. MEASURE IT before m_volca is trusted -- items 190 and 226., f 60;
#X text 20 1080 WHAT IS NOT HERE: aftertouch and pitch bend \, which the Volca ignores in any firmware \; clock and transport \, which are u_tempo's and already reach every port \; and any notion of what a note MEANS. This file is told what to play and plays it., f 84;
#X text 900 1080 ⚠️ REQUIRES PAJEN 1.09 FIRMWARE for velocity and program change -- and BOTH are gated behind global settings that no secondary source documents. Md UEL On \, PCMId On \, PCnot OFF. See ref-midi.md., f 60;
